 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How are you? Lots of people do. A typical adult human needs at least thirty minute breaks every four or five hours. Taking them improves productivity in the long run. The problem is people often take shorter, fewer breaks. That backfires badly. Something quick and easy, usually. A quick cup of tea, walk around the block, or a few jumping jacks. Probably not scrolling social is the break is the point. Something active and relaxing. You' welcome. Lots of people never take proper breaks.",
